[2026.09.08-03.57.41:766][845]LogVoxelSky: VoxelSky star map handedness RESOLVED: StarUDirection=+1.0 (read back from /Game/Voxel/MPC_VoxelSky.MPC_VoxelSky, raw +1.000), so StarRotation is being driven as +1.0 * (LST/360 + 0.0000 turns). Flipping the MPC scalar mirrors the map AND re-signs this drive together; driving +LST against a -1 map would rotate the sky backwards.
[2026.09.08-03.57.41:766][845]LogVoxelSky: VoxelSky StarAmbientGain RESOLVED to 1.0000, DERIVED from kStarAmbientCalibration (voxel.Sky.StarAmbientGain requested -1.0000; written into /Game/Voxel/MPC_VoxelSky.MPC_VoxelSky). Derived means appearance and illumination cannot drift apart unnoticed; the constant was measured at voxel.Sky.StarGain 0.15 against a snowfield whose ground/sky luminance ratio came out 0.790, i.e. snow's albedo. This is the SkyLight capture's star gain ONLY -- it cannot change a main-view pixel, because M_SkyAtmosphereDome routes it through a ReflectionCapturePassSwitch. It is the RATIO of capture star radiance to visible star radiance: voxel.Sky.StarGain (0.1500 here) is already inside the shared StarBrightness scalar both domes multiply, so this number carries none of it. 0 removes starlight from the ambient term entirely. Re-measure with tools/sky-albedo-check.py on a starlit capture: ground/sky luminance must equal the ground's albedo.
